<!-- The Tech victory's seven pieces (docs/ideas.md, Victory paths; GV 2F). heromedel, 2026-11-14: the pieces are
     goals, not destinations. Each is that race's own version of a real system, so it can come from any of that
     race's ships (bought, salvaged, demanded in a surrender, stolen), its stores or its events; with luck all seven
     could be bought along the way. The Malphen piece is never sold; the Mecha part with theirs only for a good deal.
     system: the system a piece is. A piece counts when a ship of the squad has that system and it is that race's
     make, or when the piece is in the squad's hold. The Mecha Hull Reinforcement has no system in the game yet, so
     it is only ever carried in the hold.
     Names and lines: Infall: Lori (Ai-Generated-Proposal, 2026-11-14).
     Prices and chances: Infall: Eco (Ai-Generated-Proposal, 2026-11-14, economy finding F16): a piece costs what a
     core system does, 36.31, times the band adjustment; the Mecha's good deal is 1.5 times that; a ship left whole
     carries its race's piece 1 time in 5 before band 6 and 1 in 3 from it. wreck_chance, a piece pulled from a
     wreck, is Infall: Godot Version's stand-in.
     pair: docs/ideas.md's requirement idea (2026-10-21): "one from each pair: power core or clone bay; engine or
     autopilot; shield or reinforcements; archive or genetic diversity". The setting Tech Victory Pieces chooses
     between one of each pair and all seven. Either way the pieces must all be fitted to one ship (heromedel,
     2026-11-14: "all on one ship, not just in the squad"). own_crew: the Record pair's other half, genetic
     diversity, stands in as that many living crew of the squad's own race aboard that ship (Ai-Generated-Proposal;
     the docs say "maybe 3 males and 3 females of your core race", and the game has no crew sex).
     goal_bands_from_rim: how many bands before the last the goal's event comes (band 6 of 8). demand_band: the first
     band where a surrendering ship can be asked for its piece. -->
